            <h1>The agency that kept making things that had never existed before.</h1>
            <section>
                <h2>The situation</h2>
                <p>Make Us Proud was a small London agency with an unusual brief: work at the edge of what's possible, with clients who wanted to do something genuinely new. That meant early-stage startup work — finding the problem worth solving, shaping the product, getting to v1 — alongside cultural institutions with ambitions that outpaced their technical teams.</p>
                <p>I joined [year] and stayed [duration]. In that time we worked on [number] projects, most of them the first of their kind.</p>
